<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Munza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1873</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Munza was a king of the Mangbetu in the Uele region of north-eastern Congo. The German explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georg-schweinfurth">Georg Schweinfurth</a> visited his court in 1870 and described its great hall, music, ironwork and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> in vivid detail. Munza was killed in 1873 in fighting with Nubian traders from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> and their local allies, and his kingdom broke apart.</p></div>
